ations. Currently, I'm using `remove(0)` and `insert(0, ...)` which are O(n). But for the internal computation, this is fine. The output is correct as long as the stack operations are correct.\n\nBut wait, I'm not using `remove(0)` and `insert(0, ...)` for `ra` and `rra`. I'm using a loop to shift elements. Let me verify:\n\n```rust\nfn ra(a: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    if a.len() >= 2 {\n        let first = a[0];\n        let mut i = 0;\n        while i + 1 < a.len() {\n            a[i] = a[i + 1];\n            i += 1;\n        }\n        a[a.len() - 1] = first;\n        println!(\"ra\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis shifts all elements left by 1, and puts the first element at the end. This is correct for `ra`.\n\n```rust\nfn rra(a: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    if a.len() >= 2 {\n        let last = a[a.len() - 1];\n        let mut i = a.len() - 1;\n        while i > 0 {\n            a[i] = a[i - 1];\n            i -= 1;\n        }\n        a[0] = last;\n        println!(\"rra\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis shifts all elements right by 1, and puts the last element at the beginning. This is correct for `rra`.\n\nGood.\n\nNow let me write the complete code. I'll also add `rb` and `rrb` similarly.\n\nFor `pb` and `pa`, I'll use `remove(0)` and `insert(0, ...)`:\n\n```rust\nfn pb(a: &mut Vec<i32>, b: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    if !a.is_empty() {\n        let val = a.remove(0);\n        b.insert(0, val);\n        println!(\"pb\");\n    }\n}\n\nfn pa(b: &mut Vec<i32>, a: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    if !b.is_empty() {\n        let val = b.remove(0);\n        a.insert(0, val);\n        println!(\"pa\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWait, the spec says \"pb: take the top element of a and push it onto b\". The top element is at index 0. So `a.remove(0)` is correct. And `b.insert(0, val)` puts it at the top of b. Correct.\n\nSimilarly for `pa`.\n\nGood.\n\nNow let me write the complete code. I'll structure it as a single file with all functions.\n\nOne more thing: the spec says \"no unwrap()\". I need to make sure I don'