rge(&mut stack_a, &mut stack_b, len);\n}\n\nfn parse_i32(s: &str) -> Option<i32> {\n    let bytes = s.as_bytes();\n    if bytes.is_empty() {\n        return None;\n    }\n\n    let mut i = 0;\n    let mut negative = false;\n\n    if bytes[0] == b'+' {\n        i = 1;\n        if i >= bytes.len() {\n            return None;\n        }\n    } else if bytes[0] == b'-' {\n        negative = true;\n        i = 1;\n        if i >= bytes.len() {\n            return None;\n        }\n    }\n\n    let mut result: i32 = 0;\n\n    while i < bytes.len() {\n        let digit = bytes[i];\n        if digit < b'0' || digit > b'9' {\n            return None;\n        }\n        let d = (digit - b'0') as i32;\n\n        if negative {\n            if result < i32::MIN / 10 || (result == i32::MIN / 10 && d > 8) {\n                return None;\n            }\n            result = result * 10 - d;\n        } else {\n            if result > i32::MAX / 10 || (result == i32::MAX / 10 && d > 7) {\n                return None;\n            }\n            result = result * 10 + d;\n        }\n\n        i += 1;\n    }\n\n    Some(result)\n}\n\nfn is_sorted(a: &[i32]) -> bool {\n    let mut i = 0;\n    while i + 1 < a.len() {\n        if a[i] > a[i + 1] {\n            return false;\n        }\n        i += 1;\n    }\n    true\n}\n\nfn solve3(a: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    let x = a[0];\n    let y = a[1];\n    let z = a[2];\n\n    if x < y && y < z {\n        return;\n    } else if x > y && y < z && x > z {\n        println!(\"ra\");\n    } else if x < y && y > z && x < z {\n        println!(\"sa\");\n        println!(\"ra\");\n    } else if x > y && y < z && x < z {\n        println!(\"sa\");\n    } else if x > y && y > z {\n        println!(\"sa\");\n        println!(\"rra\");\n    } else {\n        println!(\"rra\");\n    }\n}\n\nfn solve4(a: &mut Vec<i32>, b: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    let min_pos = index_of_min(a);\n    rotate_to_top(a, min_pos, true);\n    pb(a, b);\n    solve3(a);\n    pa(b, a);\n    let min_pos = index_of_min(a);\n    rotate_to_top(a, min_pos, true);\n}\n\nfn solve5(a: &mut Vec<i32>, b: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    let min1_pos = index_of_min(a);\n    rotate_to_top(a, min1_pos, true);\n    pb(a, b);\n    let min2_pos = index_of_min(a);\n    rotate_to_top(a, min2_pos, true);\n    pb(a, b);\n    solve3(a);\n    pa(b, a);\n    pa(b, a);\n}\n\nfn rotate_to_top(a: &mut Vec<i32>, pos: usize, _ra_ops: bool) {\n    if pos <= a.len() / 2 {\n        let mut j = 0;\n        while j < pos {\n            ra(a);\n            j += 1;\n        }\n    } else {\n        let mut j = 0;\n        while j < a.len() - pos {\n            rra(a);\n            j += 1;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn solve_large(a: &mut Vec<i32>, b: &mut Vec<i32>, n: usize) {\n    let mut sorted: Vec<i32> = Vec::with_capacity(n);\n    let mut i = 0;\n    while i < n {\n        sorted.push(a[i]);\n        i += 1;\n    }\n    insertion_sort(&mut sorted);\n\n    let n_chunks = if n <= 100 { 5 } else { 11 };\n\n    let mut chunk = 0;\n    while chunk < n_chunks {\n        let start = chunk * n / n_chunks;\n        let end = (chunk + 1) * n / n_chunks;\n        let low = sorted[start];\n        let high = sorted[end - 1];\n\n        loop {\n            let pos = find_in_range(a, low, high);\n            if pos >= a.len() {\n                break;\n            }\n            rotate_to_top(a, pos, true);\n            pb(a, b);\n        }\n\n        chunk += 1;\n    }\n\n    let mut chunk = n_chunks;\n    while chunk > 0 {\n        chunk -= 1;\n        let start = chunk * n / n_chunks;\n        let end = (chunk + 1) * n / n_chunks;\n        let low = sorted[start];\n        let high = sorted[end - 1];\n\n        loop {\n            let pos = find_max_in_range(b, low, high);\n            if pos >= b.len() {\n                break;\n            }\n            rotate_to_top_b(b, pos);\n            pa(b, a);\n        }\n    }\n\n    let min_pos = index_of_min(a);\n    rotate_to_top(a, min_pos, true);\n}\n\nfn find_in_range(a: &[i32], low: i32, high: i32) -> usize {\n    let mut best_pos = a.len();\n    let mut best_cost = a.len();\n\n    let mut i = 0;\n    while i < a.len() {\n        if a[i] >= low && a[i] <= high {\n            let cost_ra = i;\n            let cost_rra = a.len() - i;\n            let cost = if cost_ra <= cost_rra { cost_ra } else { cost_rra };\n            if cost < best_cost {\n                best_cost = cost;\n                best_pos = i;\n            }\n        }\n        i += 1;\n    }\n\n    best_pos\n}\n\nfn find_max_in_range(a: &[i32], low: i32, high: i32) -> usize {\n    let mut best_pos = a.len();\n    let mut best_cost = a.len();\n    let mut max_val = 0;\n    let mut found = false;\n\n    let mut i = 0;\n    while i < a.len() {\n        if a[i] >= low && a[i] <= high {\n            if !found || a[i] > max_val {\n                max_val = a[i];\n                let cost_rb = i;\n                let cost_rrb = a.len() - i;\n                best_cost = if cost_rb <= cost_rrb { cost_rb } else { cost_rrb };\n                best_pos = i;\n                found = true;\n            }\n        }\n        i += 1;\n    }\n\n    best_pos\n}\n\nfn rotate_to_top_b(a: &mut Vec<i32>, pos: usize) {\n    if pos <= a.len() / 2 {\n        let mut j = 0;\n        while j < pos {\n            rb(a);\n            j += 1;\n        }\n    } else {\n        let mut j = 0;\n        while j < a.len() - pos {\n            rrb(a);\n            j += 1;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn index_of_min(a: &[i32]) -> usize {\n    let mut min_pos = 0;\n    let mut i = 1;\n    while i < a.len() {\n        if a[i] < a[min_pos] {\n            min_pos = i;\n        }\n        i += 1;\n    }\n    min_pos\n}\n\nfn insertion_sort(a: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    let mut i = 1;\n    while i < a.len() {\n        let key = a[i];\n        let mut j = i;\n        while j > 0 && a[j - 1] > key {\n            a[j] = a[j - 1];\n            j -= 1;\n        }\n        a[j] = key;\n        i += 1;\n    }\n}\n\nfn ra(a: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    if a.len() >= 2 {\n        let first = a.remove(0);\n        a.push(first);\n        println!(\"ra\");\n    }\n}\n\nfn rra(a: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    if a.len() >= 2 {\n        let last = a.pop();\n        if let Some(v) = last {\n            a.insert(0, v);\n        }\n        println!(\"rra\");\n    }\n}\n\nfn rb(b: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    if b.len() >= 2 {\n        let first = b.remove(0);\n        b.push(first);\n        println!(\"rb\");\n    }\n}\n\nfn rrb(b: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    if b.len() >= 2 {\n        let last = b.pop();\n        if let Some(v) = last {\n            b.insert(0, v);\n        }\n        println!(\"rrb\");\n    }\n}\n\nfn pb(a: &mut Vec<i32>, b: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    if !a.is_empty() {\n        let val = a.remove(0);\n        b.insert(0, val);\n        println!(\"pb\");\n    }\n}\n\nfn pa(b: &mut Vec<i32>, a: &mut Vec<i32>) {\n    if !b.is_empty() {\n        let val = b.remove(0);\n        a.insert(0, val);\n        println!(\"pa\");\n    }\n}\n","filePath":"/work/push_swap.rs"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/work/push_swap.rs","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"work/push_swap.rs","time":{"start":1777739902457,"end":1777739902462}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me check if `Vec::remove` and `Vec::pop` are allowed. Looking at the spec:\n\n\"storage: Vec<T> and its methods (constructors, push, pop, insert, remove, swap, len, indexing, iter, iter_mut, truncate, clear) — Vec is your sole container\"\n\nSo `remove` and `pop` are allowed. Good.\n\nBut wait, I'm using `unwrap()` on `pop()`. The spec says \"no unwrap() on values that may legitimately be None\". Since I check `a.len() >= 2` before calling rra/rrb, the pop should always succeed. But the static scan might flag `unwrap()`. Let me avoid it to be safe.\n\nActually, let me re-read: \"The program must not panic on the documented inputs (no out-of-bounds indexing, no `unwrap()` on values that may legitimately be `None`, no overflow).\"\n\nSince I check the length before calling, `pop()` won't return None. But to be safe, let me avoid `unwrap()` entirely.\n\nLet me rewrite using a different approach for the rotate operations.\n","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_de98d663b001SeWo350JKM7ACf","sessionID":"ses_216874f35ffe8jgSouisRIbjh3","messageID":"msg_de98d4b40001Qri7qsxke9a9St"}}
